1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,409
Two shots, a stone's throw from help.

2
00:00:02,639 --> 00:00:05,985
Lake Station, 1888, as a Chesterton paper

3
00:00:05,995 --> 00:00:06,659
reported it.

4
00:00:07,209 --> 00:00:10,036
George Wolf was 72, feeble, partly deaf,

5
00:00:10,046 --> 00:00:10,992
and home alone.

6
00:00:11,222 --> 00:00:12,813
His wife was away caring for a

7
00:00:12,823 --> 00:00:14,352
granddaughter, the paper said.

8
00:00:14,902 --> 00:00:17,362
The paper put his house west of town,

9
00:00:17,372 --> 00:00:20,087
about 250 feet north of the Michigan

10
00:00:20,097 --> 00:00:20,760
Central tracks.

11
00:00:21,310 --> 00:00:24,392
About 7:30 that Sunday evening, a freight

12
00:00:24,402 --> 00:00:26,367
train was switching cars in front of the

13
00:00:26,377 --> 00:00:26,653
house.

14
00:00:26,883 --> 00:00:28,497
The trainmen heard two shots.

15
00:00:29,346 --> 00:00:31,002
Railroad men went to the house.

16
00:00:31,232 --> 00:00:33,306
George Wolf had been murdered in his own

17
00:00:33,316 --> 00:00:33,749
doorway.

18
00:00:34,399 --> 00:00:35,636
No weapon was found.

19
00:00:35,866 --> 00:00:38,655
The coroner's verdict: murder, probably by

20
00:00:38,665 --> 00:00:38,973
tramps.

21
00:00:39,523 --> 00:00:41,549
The paper called it shrouded in mystery.

22
00:00:41,779 --> 00:00:44,103
Months later, when his widow died, it

23
00:00:44,113 --> 00:00:45,812
still called it a mysterious murder.

24
00:00:46,462 --> 00:00:48,505
Comment your town, and it could be next.

